{
  "mark.6.p1.b1": {
    "text": "Jesus went on from there and came to His hometown, accompanied by His disciples.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:1"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p1.b2": {
    "text": "Where did this man get these ideas?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:2"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p1.b3": {
    "text": "What is this wisdom He has been given?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:2"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p1.b4": {
    "text": "And how can He perform such miracles?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:2"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p2.b1": {
    "text": "Isn’t this the carpenter,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:3"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p2.b2": {
    "text": "The son of Mary and the brother of James, Joses, Judas, and Simon?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:3"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p2.b3": {
    "text": "Aren’t His sisters here with us as well?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:3"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p2.b4": {
    "text": "And they took offense at Him.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:3"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p3.b1": {
    "text": "Only in his hometown, among his relatives, and in his own household is a prophet without honor.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:4"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p3.b2": {
    "text": "So He could not perform any miracles there, except to lay His hands on a few of the sick and heal them.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:5"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p3.b3": {
    "text": "And He was amazed at their unbelief. And He went around from village to village, teaching the people.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:6"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p4.b1": {
    "text": "Then Jesus called the Twelve to Him and began to send them out two by two,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:7"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p4.b2": {
    "text": "Giving them authority over unclean spirits.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:7"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p4.b3": {
    "text": "No bread, no bag, no money in their belts",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:8"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p4.b4": {
    "text": "He instructed them to take nothing but a staff for the journey",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:8"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p5.b1": {
    "text": "When you enter a house,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:10"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p5.b2": {
    "text": "Stay there until you leave that area.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:10"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p5.b3": {
    "text": "If anyone will not welcome you or listen to you,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:11"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p5.b4": {
    "text": "Shake the dust off your feet when you leave that place, as a testimony against them.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:11"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p6.b1": {
    "text": "So they set out and preached",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:12"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p6.b2": {
    "text": "That the people should repent.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:12"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p6.b3": {
    "text": "They also drove out many demons",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:13"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p6.b4": {
    "text": "And healed many of the sick, anointing them with oil.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:13"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p7.b1": {
    "text": "John the Baptist has risen from the dead!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:14"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p7.b2": {
    "text": "He is Elijah,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:15"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p7.b3": {
    "text": "He is a prophet, like one of the prophets of old.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:15"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p7.b4": {
    "text": "John, whom I beheaded, has risen from the dead!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:16"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p8.b1": {
    "text": "On account of his brother Philip’s wife Herodias, whom Herod had married.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:17"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p8.b2": {
    "text": "It is not lawful for you to have your brother’s wife!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:18"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p8.b3": {
    "text": "So Herodias held a grudge against John and wanted to kill him. But she had been unable,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:19"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p8.b4": {
    "text": "Because Herod feared John and protected him, knowing that he was a righteous and holy man.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:20"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p9.b1": {
    "text": "On Herod’s birthday, her opportunity arose. Herod held a banquet for his nobles and military commanders and the leading men of Galilee.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:21"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p9.b2": {
    "text": "When the daughter of Herodias came and danced, she pleased Herod and his guests,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:22"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p9.b3": {
    "text": "Ask me for whatever you wish, and I will give it to you.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:22"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p9.b4": {
    "text": "Whatever you ask of me, I will give you, up to half my kingdom!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:23"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p10.b1": {
    "text": "What should I request?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:24"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p10.b2": {
    "text": "The head of John the Baptist.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:24"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p10.b3": {
    "text": "I want you to give me the head of John the Baptist on a platter immediately.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:25"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p11.b1": {
    "text": "The king was consumed with sorrow, but because of his oaths and his guests, he did not want to refuse her.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:26"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p11.b2": {
    "text": "So without delay, the king commanded that John’s head be brought in. He sent an executioner,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:27"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p11.b3": {
    "text": "Who went and beheaded him in the prison.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:27"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p11.b4": {
    "text": "…the girl, who gave it to her mother.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:28"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p12.b1": {
    "text": "When John’s disciples heard about this,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:29"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p12.b2": {
    "text": "They came and took his body",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:29"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p12.b3": {
    "text": "And placed it in a tomb.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:29"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p13.b1": {
    "text": "Meanwhile, the apostles gathered around Jesus and brought Him news of all they had done and taught.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:30"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p13.b2": {
    "text": "Come with Me privately to a solitary place, and let us rest for a while.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:31"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p13.b3": {
    "text": "For many people were coming and going, and they did not even have time to eat.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:31"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p13.b4": {
    "text": "So they went away in a boat by themselves to a solitary place.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:32"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p14.b1": {
    "text": "They ran together on foot from all the towns and arrived before them.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:33"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p14.b2": {
    "text": "When Jesus stepped ashore and saw a large crowd, He had compassion on them,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:34"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p14.b3": {
    "text": "Because they were like sheep without a shepherd.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:34"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p14.b4": {
    "text": "And He began to teach them many things.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:34"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p15.b1": {
    "text": "This is a desolate place, and the hour is already late.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:35"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p15.b2": {
    "text": "Dismiss the crowd so they can go to the surrounding countryside and villages and buy themselves something to eat.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:36"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p15.b3": {
    "text": "You give them something to eat.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:37"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p15.b4": {
    "text": "Should we go out and spend two hundred denarii to give all of them bread to eat?",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:37"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p16.b1": {
    "text": "Go and see how many loaves you have,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:38"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p16.b2": {
    "text": "Five—and two fish.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:38"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p16.b3": {
    "text": "Then Jesus directed them to have the people sit in groups on the green grass.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:39"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p16.b4": {
    "text": "So they sat down in groups of hundreds and fifties.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:40"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p17.b1": {
    "text": "Taking the five loaves and the two fish and looking up to heaven, Jesus spoke a blessing",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:41"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p17.b2": {
    "text": "And broke the loaves. Then He gave them to His disciples",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:41"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p17.b3": {
    "text": "To set before the people. And He divided the two fish among them all.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:41"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p18.b1": {
    "text": "They all ate and were satisfied,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:42"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p18.b2": {
    "text": "And the disciples picked up twelve basketfuls of broken pieces of bread and fish.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:43"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p18.b3": {
    "text": "And there were five thousand men who had eaten the loaves.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:44"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p19.b1": {
    "text": "Immediately Jesus made His disciples get into the boat and go on ahead of Him to Bethsaida, while He dismissed the crowd.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:45"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p19.b2": {
    "text": "After bidding them farewell, He went up on the mountain to pray.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:46"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p19.b3": {
    "text": "When evening came,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:47"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p19.b4": {
    "text": "The boat was in the middle of the sea, and Jesus was alone on land.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:47"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p20.b1": {
    "text": "He could see that the disciples were straining to row, because the wind was against them.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:48"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p20.b2": {
    "text": "About the fourth watch of the night,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:48"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p20.b3": {
    "text": "Jesus went out to them, walking on the sea.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:48"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p20.b4": {
    "text": "He intended to pass by them,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:48"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p21.b1": {
    "text": "But when they saw Him walking on the sea, … thinking He was a ghost",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:49"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p21.b2": {
    "text": "They cried out, … for they all saw Him and were terrified.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:49-50"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p21.b3": {
    "text": "Take courage!",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:50"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p21.b4": {
    "text": "It is I. Do not be afraid.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:50"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p22.b1": {
    "text": "And the wind died down.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:51"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p22.b2": {
    "text": "And the disciples were utterly astounded,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:51"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p22.b3": {
    "text": "For they had not understood about the loaves,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:52"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p22.b4": {
    "text": "But their hearts had been hardened.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:52"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p23.b1": {
    "text": "When they had crossed over, they landed at Gennesaret and moored the boat.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:53"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p23.b2": {
    "text": "As soon as they got out of the boat, the people recognized Jesus",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:54"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p23.b3": {
    "text": "And ran through that whole region,",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:55"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p23.b4": {
    "text": "Carrying the sick on mats to wherever they heard He was.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:55"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p24.b1": {
    "text": "And wherever He went—villages and towns and countrysides",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:56"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p24.b2": {
    "text": "They laid the sick in the marketplaces",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:56"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p24.b3": {
    "text": "And begged Him just to let them touch the fringe of His cloak.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:56"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  },
  "mark.6.p24.b4": {
    "text": "And all who touched Him were healed.",
    "kind": "scripture",
    "source": {
      "version": "engbsb",
      "ref": "Mark 6:56"
    },
    "adapted": false,
    "status": "approved"
  }
}
